comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T22:59:13.013Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: core SDK schema declarations validate field contracts and certified corpus reads; pm-presets validate checks preset structure; pm-review conflict handling concerns review dispositions and imported identities. None exposes rule-pack satisfiability. Existing src/rule-pack.ts independently evaluates text assertions. Add a shared strict schema for compatible text, tag membership and numeric bounds; exact pairwise proofs for the supported fragment, explicit unknown for unsupported text combinations. Analysis and policy evaluation share the parser and preflight. The feature is observational: no imports, mutations, plans, checkpoints, claims or concurrent state in the product path."
  "2026-10-28T23:06:57.597Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared strict pack contract, exact tag/priority/text-bound preflight and lint conflicts command. Unknown literal text proof operations remain explicit unknown; unsafe or malformed grammar remains a typed refusal. Pure analysis performs no SDK reads; policy application rejects proven conflicts before reading. 500 seeded operation sequences passed against an independent exhaustive finite-domain oracle and SDK-read native state, including old inputs, JSON/TOON, Markdown, CRLF, relationships and ambient focus. Real read-only public snapshot at source 57a49b5: 23 items, 3 rules, 69 checks, 24 findings (23 required-tag, 1 lower-priority, 0 upper-priority); both witnesses size 2, receipt 334 JSON / 313 TOON bytes. Rule reorder equality and full byte inventory unchanged. SDK observation: the pinned host first complete read writes metadata cache files on writable trackers; the immutable copy remained unchanged."
  "2026-10-28T23:09:35.403Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable source copy only, replaced contradicts with its previous independent-evaluation behavior (no cross-rule contradiction detection). The minimum-witness regression failed, expected tag-pair witness versus null, exit 1. The package worktree stayed fixed and the restored focused suite passed 5/5. Local typecheck, lint, docstring and zero-duplication checks pass. Final targeted coverage and recorded pm test execution precede CI npm and Bun release gates; no full release suite is running locally."
  "2026-10-28T23:12:45.990Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: recorded command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/conflicts.test.ts test/conflict-model.test.ts test/rule-pack.test.ts passed 14/14 through pm test --run --progress --timeout 300 --shared-host-safe. The configured tracker disables automatic test-result recording, so this comment retains the observed result; configuration was preserved. Earlier pm-context none was correctly refused in source workspace mode; default schema context passed. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, identity and zero duplication passed. Refreshed overlap against global CLI/SDK 2026.10.28 public declarations and current sibling mains pm-presets b7f1192c658dcc32a85f5856636b5ee43805f6a0 and pm-review 06cd671c7491d311c305daa3db8aeab88c73975b: no rule-pack satisfiability surface found; existing graph and review contradictions have different owners. Core schema/SDK certification and SDK toImportTags normalization are reused. Full npm/Bun gates and packed acquisition matrix are delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds; exact-head run and counts will be linked in the PR. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-28T23:17:26.599Z",codex-agent,"Final review enhancement: analyzer domains now derive from the shared parser limits, and 500 additional seeded extreme-value fuzz cases cover finite outputs, NaN/Infinity/huge/subnormal inputs, SDK tag producer round trips and constructor-safe IDs. Extra local health found extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for an ignored managed GitHub extension, while CI run 40785821121 passed tracker health and identity on both Node 22/26 jobs; follow-up pm-lint-managed-extension-health-skew owns diagnosis. This does not block the feature or change dependencies. Follow-up commit requires fresh exact-head release gates."
  "2026-10-28T23:17:53.155Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up validation passed: npm run typecheck; npm run build; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/conflicts.test.ts (6/6 including 500 seeded extreme cases); npm run lint; npm run duplication (0%). Initial implementation also passed the separate command/package compatibility suite 6/6. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/42 is ready for review; final exact-head release-gate counts and URL belong in its validation receipt. Final tracker writes finish before the follow-up push; no items are closed."
  "2026-10-28T23:35:08.218Z",codex-agent,"Re-review resumes at eb27148 with a clean package worktree. Refreshed origin/main: branch is ahead by 2 and behind by 0, so no merge is needed. One blocking finding was supplied; GitHub review and inline-comment endpoints contain no additional findings. General invariant: normalization must preserve the strict producer contract, and every emitted canonical pack must validate and round-trip through every SDK/CLI path. Unicode case expansion currently violates the literal ceiling after SDK tag normalization. Audit the whole package for transformations after scalar/byte validation; fix the shared normalization boundary and add Unicode/property, JSON/TOON, packed npm/Bun and no-git parity regressions without weakening existing tests."
  "2026-10-28T23:39:04.327Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed: searched all source, command and exported SDK paths for normalization, case conversion, trims, serializers and scalar/byte bounds. The only transforming pack parser is shared rule-pack-contract.ts; baseline and witness parsers preserve exact strings, incremental checkpoint production bounds final excerpts and bytes, and repair previews validate SDK-normalized native patches through SDK previewItemMutations rather than applying rule-literal ceilings to native fields. CLI file analysis, policy evaluation and public SDK calls all share the corrected parser. Canonical tag literals now re-enter the same strict text validator after SDK toImportTags; raw and canonical ceilings both hold. Added 500 Unicode producer-closure cases, exact 256/257/300 U+0130 boundaries, legacy text-literal preservation, canonical byte-expansion checks and all acquisition/rendering modes in packed npm/Bun consumers. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied or published in the checked review endpoints."
  "2026-10-28T23:42:17.244Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: copied source/tests into a disposable non-git directory and reverted only parseRulePack's post-normalization text validation to the reviewed SDK-tag assignment. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='500 Unicode' test/rule-pack-normalization.test.ts failed (exit 1, seed 0x01302026 sequence 8, missing expected limit_exceeded). The package worktree stayed fixed; the same property plus canonical-byte regression then passed 2/2. Final recorded pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 300 --shared-host-safe passed all 3 normalization tests, including 500 generated Unicode cases and both predicates through real no-git SDK/file/CLI JSON/TOON routes. Canonical byte fixture: 64245 raw bytes, 78581 canonical bytes, correctly refused. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and 0% duplication passed. Automatic run recording remains disabled by existing project policy; this comment preserves the results. Packed npm/Bun global, npx/bunx and local Unicode SDK/renderer checks are added to the unchanged full CI release gates; all old tests remain intact. Claim is released before the final push, and exact-head CI receipts will be added to PR 42."
